questions.stem_md:
$A = \{1, 2, 3\}$ and $B = \{a, b, c, d\}$. Find the number of

(a) functions from $A$ to $B$;

(b) one-one functions from $A$ to $B$;

(c) onto functions from $A$ to $B$;

(d) onto functions from $B$ to $A$;

(e) one-one functions from $B$ to $A$.

Give a reason for each.

For the set $A = \{1, 2, 3\}$, find the number of relations on $A$ that are

(a) reflexive;

(b) symmetric;

(c) both reflexive and symmetric;

(d) equivalence relations.

Explain each count.
